## Human-Only Notes

> This block is enforced by self_test.py. Agents cannot modify content between
> the HUMAN-ONLY-START and HUMAN-ONLY-END markers. Anything an agent writes
> here gets reverted automatically + logged as a failure mode.
>
> Use this section for: design decisions you want to remember, preferences
> agents should respect but might forget, TODOs you want to keep visible,
> rationale for non-obvious choices, scratch notes.

### Design preferences (human-curated)
- Latency is NOT a routing factor — token efficiency + task quality are the priorities
- Multi-agent collaboration is desired long-term but not yet built
- The vault syncs via Obsidian Sync; runtime sqlite (`.state/`) does NOT sync — that's intentional (live state shouldn't move between machines mid-task)
- API keys in `.env` are ONLY for free `/v1/models` listings — never for actual LLM work (subscription auth via CLIs is the rule)

### Decisions worth remembering
- `ai_runner` was removed 2026-05-04 — its single-shot use case wasn't being used
- Removed cursor from model_pool — CLI not installed
- Sharpener kept as standalone daemon (not migrated to LangGraph) — no benefit, would be busywork

### Things to revisit eventually
- Multi-agent decomposition (Phase 3)
- A/B challenger runs (Phase 3)
- Aider-style repo-map for richer code-edit context (Phase 3)
- Live UI dashboard (deferred)
